{"title":"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_1.5,_half_(desperate)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1.5, half (desperate)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_2:_Full_Thinking_Process_of_Solution_1.5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2: Full Thinking Process of Solution 1.5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_3:_Clarification_of_Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3: Clarification of Solution 1</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Note\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Note</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Comment\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Comment</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the largest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />-digit <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a> factor of the integer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/f/b1fbff8e51d2276c16f2df37d3e90dfcb6bff5d6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = {200\\choose 100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"86\" height=\"53\" />?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Expanding the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Combination\" title=\"Combination\">binomial coefficient</a>, we get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/0/6a0878c7099e6010773953a532552ccadd6ec9de.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${200 \\choose 100}=\\frac{200!}{100!100!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -22px\" width=\"146\" height=\"53\" />. Let the required prime be <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />; then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/2/b5216c44c1ce1e99401c0009d1c31585d4a343dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10 \\le p &lt; 100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"102\" height=\"16\" />. If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/3/2/932901acb132dfcb0bf859910abad37569852196.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p &gt; 50$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"52\" height=\"16\" />, then the factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> appears twice in the denominator. Thus, we need <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to appear as a factor at least three times in the numerator, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/a/a/5aa0b845f1bc8509b66002a9fe457f09d09cd890.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3p&lt;200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"69\" height=\"16\" />. The largest such prime is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/0/67011f852e18a5c927e5dbc7765491bb88da153f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{061}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"39\" height=\"23\" />, which is our answer.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_1.5.2C_half_.28desperate.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1.5,_half_(desperate)\">Solution 1.5, half (desperate)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1.5, half (desperate)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>The only way a single prime number will be left out after all the cancelation will have to satisfy the condition that out of all the multiples of the prime number we want to find, 2 of the multiples will have to be between 100 and 200, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" /> is good for this solution (if you know your primes) because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/7/517c6d163ec38d9bc469bbd1c92620c665943a74.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61 \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/3/e/d3e2601e1b374b7d3be9efed92627fdd7f472504.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" /> both lie in the interval <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/7/6a7bbc83ff66c7a504e14b594fe8354c4599140e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(100, 200)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"79\" height=\"20\" />.\n</p><p>The reason for this is because if 2 copies of the prime <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> we want to find are on the numerator and one copy on the denominator (AKA it contains <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/1/591f689f950feb4a9cff58ff3166d915f916a405.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"16\" height=\"18\" /> and also <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/b/b4be132dae3ab5e83bc11adc4371f0c9c856a2a4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\dfrac{1}{p}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -17px\" width=\"15\" height=\"42\" />), there will only be 1 copy of the prime we want to find when all the cancellation is made when reducing the original fraction (only <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is left after cancellation).\n</p><p><br />\n~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/1/b/61bcd4a65d4aca6ec6a56ad608b184b2f68065dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Michaellin16$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"111\" height=\"14\" /> (formatted shalomkeshet)\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2:_Full_Thinking_Process_of_Solution_1.5\">Solution 2: Full Thinking Process of Solution 1.5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2: Full Thinking Process of Solution 1.5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We want the largest two‑digit prime factor of\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/c/33c0651b8bdb5458420bf5ba5fa6f4f6fb3b7bd9.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{200\\choose100}=\\frac{200\\cdot199\\cdot\\ldots\\cdot101}{100\\cdot99\\cdot\\ldots\\cdot1}.\\]\" width=\"225\" height=\"53\" />\n</p><p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> be a two‑digit prime factor of this number. Any such <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that remains after cancellation must appear at least twice in the numerator, because one factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in a multiple of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the numerator will cancel with itself in the denominator. Therefore, there must be at least two multiples of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/b/94bb6fb7a3ff722532798b45607025254679e7b2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/f/3/8f37626d49b4082c9102bf930bca51277ff2eb43.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"29\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>Write such a multiple as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a21f1a661365b5a7654a5528cf627f33344f8e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kp$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" />, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> is a positive integer. Then\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36fedbe06504b8739dca0de585682d698261f81f.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[101\\le kp\\le200.\\]\" width=\"123\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is two‑digit, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/0/0/f0049f8bb8a30aee27ae07a37decc4085ca6fd8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$10\\le p\\le99$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"96\" height=\"17\" />. Dividing the inequality by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> gives\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/d/a/7da609a5e92637d77d55ce2da4c14c073c59e9d1.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac{101}{k}\\le p\\le\\frac{200}{k}.\\]\" width=\"121\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/e/d/5ed8470bc717a49aafe4556c7e2c2e11ddc7b687.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/5/4750253403deed4b4a78cbe10cc1c0e022b68a99.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{101}{1}\\le p\\le\\frac{200}{1}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/c/d5ccbc86bc0528ddf3741c7cb6ae1a7622ad646a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$101\\le p\\le200$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"114\" height=\"17\" />, impossible because <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is two‑digit.\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/0/d/80d6d993e99d32e9a5641f75adc3c6665d71c2eb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{101}{2}\\le p\\le\\frac{200}{2}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/6/8a6ec2fdfc5c45b3edbba5a078251b89b9884824.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$50.5\\le p\\le100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"119\" height=\"17\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/4/7/9473603e8a0344f2b2706dc51faa3ddaba3feacf.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[51\\le p\\le99.\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p>For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/1/c/71c3e279326744c2b31ca3da43cb05ef88a497e4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{101}{3}\\le p\\le\\frac{200}{3}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"122\" height=\"38\" />, which gives <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/c/79cc7bccae0dedf50ac66d03a0f441cf56f83d8d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$33.67\\le p\\le66.67$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"142\" height=\"17\" />, so\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/9/c/a9c197c1fbf951a3ba7f73cf82b62fd4ac0df51e.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[34\\le p\\le66.\\]\" width=\"96\" height=\"15\" />\n</p><p>Notice that for larger <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" />, the upper bound is smaller, so larger <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> minimize the maximum possible value of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Thus the possible range of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> that has at least two multiples in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/2/6c2c0e6b09facf31fafc92ca3515ec622686e752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[101,200]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" /> is the intersection\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/a/a/1aa334bfad9e130f9950c92b9921f02ff172be5d.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[[51,99]\\cap[34,66]=[51,66].\\]\" width=\"209\" height=\"18\" />\n</p><p>The largest prime in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/1/ef1d3eb4388987db6a4f95c9e867fedf40885ecb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[51,66]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"56\" height=\"20\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/6/6/866b44935f69a5b800547127fe13210bb1e36fbc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$61$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"13\" />.\n</p><p>Therefore the largest two‑digit prime factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/5/d/15d1589c8d7d5545a9d1bdbce60f25183bd03c4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"${200\\choose100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"57\" height=\"55\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abdad103a89e8105327ac90f405444a09f282f1d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"31\" height=\"25\" />.\n</p><p>Note: If <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> was less than or equal to 50, then for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/a/2/6a21f1a661365b5a7654a5528cf627f33344f8e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$kp$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"21\" height=\"18\" /> would not be in the range <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/2/6c2c0e6b09facf31fafc92ca3515ec622686e752.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$[101,200]$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"75\" height=\"20\" />. But since we have found a prime greater than 50, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/f/6/4f681bd84648c174d45eed0037702cae77ed0686.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=2$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/5/3359f43f0fd0ed3b672d389374aecd0360921a47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k=3$\" width=\"43\" height=\"12\" /> works.\n</p><p><br />\n~ <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/a/5/2a542252a8babcdb9d0a29be389ed2c331a8acd0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$SS240102696$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"108\" height=\"14\" />\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3:_Clarification_of_Solution_1\">Solution 3: Clarification of Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3: Clarification of Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We know that \n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/a/c/cac11b8537859d11a4e3be8efcef3a4a67c333af.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[{200\\choose100}=\\frac{200!}{100!100!}\\]\" width=\"142\" height=\"53\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/3/5/735415f3a569b547e39da634c77f543ce049f3e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&lt;100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"61\" height=\"16\" />, there is at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/e/dce34f4dfb2406144304ad0d6106c5382ddd1446.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in each of the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/3/8/2386bdd606fd59914baef9cb493107e283003db7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$100!$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> in the denominator. Thus there must be at least <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/c/d/7cde695f2e4542fd01f860a89189f47a27143b66.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in the numerator <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/c/3ac16e40f4473566bdf830ecd45e29a671e2d701.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$200!$\" width=\"30\" height=\"13\" /> for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> to be a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/1/7/f177f416de846a0ac20ded0645006456ee9d8c18.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n=\\frac{200!}{100!100!}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"102\" height=\"38\" />. (Note that here we assume the minimum because as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> goes larger in value, the number of factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> in a number decreases,)\n</p><p>So basically, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is the largest prime number such that\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/b/d6b4bcf5fed67b290052cae032950a11ab1ad2be.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\left \\lfloor\\frac{200}{p}\\right \\rfloor&gt;3\\]\" width=\"80\" height=\"43\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/6/126c2e892af120e1495084d3abe3544526e19f5a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p&lt;\\frac{200}{3}=66.66...$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"144\" height=\"37\" />, the largest prime value for <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/6/f/36f73fc1312ee0349b3f3a0f3bd9eb5504339011.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/f/8/af8fcaec575ebc379e83486407bb348f924a20d0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$p=\\boxed{61}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"65\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~ Nafer\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Note\">Note</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Note\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Similar to 2023 MATHCOUNTS State Sprint #25\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Comment\">Comment</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Comment\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>which came first, 1985 or 2023?\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME\" title=\"1983 AIME\">1983 AIME </a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1983 AIME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=45&amp;year=1983\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_12\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 12\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1983_AIME_Problems/Problem_13\" title=\"1983 AIME Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <